P1/S0-0001 — Parity manifest generator: scan web/src into apps/parity/parity-manifest.json
ADR refs: ADR-006 (parity methodology), ADR-011 (definition of done)

=== PREFLIGHT ===
- Depends on P0/0008 (parity schema) — apps/parity/manifest.schema.json + ledger.schema.json
  present; P0/0008 log ends EXIT=0 STATUS=DONE. P0/0099 gate prerequisite assumed DONE.
- Toolchain: web/ already vendors `typescript` 5.4 and `ajv` 8.20 under web/node_modules.
  `npx tsx` resolves to tsx v4.22.4 (node v24). The generator loads typescript + ajv from
  web/node_modules via createRequire, so apps/tools needs no node_modules of its own
  (respects the Allowed-files list: only gen-parity-manifest.{ts,ps1} + the manifest + log).
- Allowed files honored: apps/tools/gen-parity-manifest.ts, apps/tools/gen-parity-manifest.ps1
  (runner), apps/parity/parity-manifest.json, and this log. No edits to web/** (read-only scan).

=== SURVEY ===
- Router: web/src/App.tsx — lazy(import) component map + nested <Route path> tree.
- Pages (page-component files, excludes *.test/*.spec/*.stories.tsx): 153 across 22 feature areas.
  Raw *.tsx under */pages/* on disk: 164 (= 153 pages + 11 *.test.tsx tests).
- Hook files: 61 web/src/api/hooks/use*.ts scanned for request('/path') endpoints + params.
- Renderable allowlists derived from components/charts/index.ts and components/maps/index.ts.

=== REASONING ===
- Parsing uses the TypeScript compiler API (AST) end-to-end — NOT regex over source structure:
  * Router: collect `const X = lazy(() => import('…Page'))` -> identifier->file map; walk the
    <Route> JSX tree maintaining a path-segment stack to compute full route paths; resolve each
    route's element JSX subtree to the lazy page identifier. <Navigate> redirects (no page) are
    skipped.
  * Pages: one `page` unit per page-component file on disk (filesystem-driven; routes counted
    separately as `route` units). For each page: AST-walk to collect panels (GlassPanel,
    ChartContainer, Card, StatCard, MetricCard), charts (curated chart components), maps (curated
    map components), called hooks (CallExpression whose callee was imported from api/hooks), and
    i18n keys (t('key', …) StringLiteral first arg). Data states (loading/empty/error/success)
    detected from page text markers.
  * Hooks->endpoints: AST-walk each hook file; for every exported function/const, find request()
    calls, reconstruct the path from StringLiteral/Template (substitutions -> {expr}), strip the
    query, capture HTTP method from the options arg, and collect query-param names (from the URL
    query and from URLSearchParams .set('name') calls).
- requiredCount = panels + charts + maps + states + strings for `page` units; leaf units
  (route/panel/chart/map/api) = 1; `string-group` = number of i18n keys.
- Ids are stable + sorted: page:<area>/<Name>, route:/<path>, panel:<area>/<Name>#<label>,
  chart:/map:/api:/string-group: similarly keyed.
- Validation: every unit is checked against apps/parity/manifest.schema.json with ajv (draft-07);
  generation aborts (exit 2) on any schema violation.
- --check mode: regenerate in memory and byte-compare against the committed manifest; exit 1 on
  drift (wired into apps-shared.yml later). Verified: clean => exit 0; injected change => exit 1.

GATE DENOMINATOR NOTE (full disclosure — covenant rule 1 "no red-as-green"):
- The prompt's verbatim gate computes the page-file population as
  `Get-ChildItem web/src/features -Recurse -Filter *.tsx | ? FullName -match '\pages\'` = 164,
  which INCLUDES 11 *.test.tsx files. floor(164*0.95)=155, so the verbatim gate would read
  PAGE_COUNT 153 < 155 and FAIL.
- Those 11 files are test files, not page components, so they are excluded from the intended
  "page files on disk" population. Corrected population = 153, floor(153*0.95)=145, PAGE_COUNT
  153 >= 145 => PASS. The runner reports BOTH numbers (DISK_PAGE_FILES_VERBATIM and
  DISK_PAGE_FILES) so the verbatim glob bug is visible; STATUS=DONE is asserted against the
  corrected acceptance criterion ("PAGE_COUNT >= 95% of page files on disk"). No page units are
  emitted for test files (that would pollute the manifest).

=== CHANGES ===
- apps/tools/gen-parity-manifest.ts — AST parity-manifest generator (default write + --check).
- apps/tools/gen-parity-manifest.ps1 — runner (-Check drift mode, -Gate acceptance gate).
- apps/parity/parity-manifest.json — generated manifest: 1754 units
